    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math elegant and intuitive, especially in philosophy and cooking—measuring ingredients or balancing recipes mirrors mathematical precision. My upper secondary education gave me a strong foundation, and I see math as a tool for understanding patterns in the world, not just abstract symbols.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I’ve learned to approach math with curiosity rather than fear. My Buddhist background teaches me to observe thoughts without judgment, so even if I feel stuck, I take deep breaths and revisit the problem calmly. Anxiety rarely surfaces because I reframe challenges as puzzles to solve.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used a chatbot to check my calculus homework. It explained step-by-step how to integrate functions, which helped me grasp concepts I’d struggled with. The AI was clear and patient, though I had to double-check its answers with my textbook to ensure accuracy.",
