    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math lessons by adapting to individual learning speeds and styles. For example, they could generate practice problems tailored to a student’s weaknesses, or explain concepts in simple analogies—like comparing derivatives to slopes of paths. This makes math more accessible and engaging."
